            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0565" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg519"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/107½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">20 February, 1917</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am glad you had this
                    talk with the ex-President and formed a favourable impression of him. His
                    explanation of the revolt is just what had formed in my own mind out of such
                    information as had reached us.</p>
                <p>I will be willing to see him, of course, as you request. It will add nothing to
                    what we already know, but it may make an impression in certain quarters which it
                    is desirable to make.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
